# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in values from your Supabase project
# (Project Settings -> API in the Supabase dashboard).

NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR-PROJECT-REF.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-public-key

# --- Optional: only needed for automatic (scheduled) calendar sync. ---
# Without these, iCal feeds still work fine via the "Sync now" / "Sync all
# feeds" buttons on the Properties page -- just not on a schedule. See
# webapp/README.md "Automatic sync" for setting up a free external
# scheduler (e.g. cron-job.org) to call /api/cron/sync-ical periodically.
#
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY bypasses Row Level Security. Keep it out of
# NEXT_PUBLIC_* (never sent to the browser), out of the repo, and only set
# it where the cron route actually runs (e.g. Vercel project env vars).
# From Project Settings -> API Keys -> the secret/service-role key.
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your-service-role-key
#
# A random secret you generate yourself (e.g. `openssl rand -hex 32`).
# Whatever calls /api/cron/sync-ical on a schedule must send it as an
# `Authorization: Bearer <value>` header -- this is how the route checks
# the request is really your own scheduled job and not the public internet.
# CRON_SECRET=

# --- Optional: only needed for push notifications. ---
# Without these, the app still works fine, and the "Enable notifications"
# button just won't appear -- see webapp/README.md "Mobile app access +
# push notifications" for how to generate your own pair with
# `npx web-push generate-vapid-keys`.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY must match VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY exactly (the
# public half is sent to the browser to subscribe; the server needs the
# same value again alongside the private key to sign outgoing pushes).
# VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY must be kept out of the repo and out of NEXT_PUBLIC_*.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=
# VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=
# VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=
# VAPID_SUBJECT=mailto:you@example.com
